Similarly, antioxidant oil additives and fuel additives are used to inhibit autoxidation. In food The prevention of autoxidation is important in the food and drink industry and is achieved both by both chemical preservatives and a range of oxygen excluding food preservation techniques such as canning . It is well known that fats, especially polyunsaturated fats , become rancid, even when kept at low temperatures, [ 19 ] however many other foods are susceptible to autoxidation.
The complex mixture of compounds found in wine, including polyphenols , polysaccharides, and proteins, can undergo autoxidation during the aging process, leading to wine faults . 
